From: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 08:46:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] drm/bridge: it66121: use dev_err_probe() on the
 supply-enable path

The it66122 bridge sits on i2c0 together with the tps65217 PMIC that
provides its vcn33/vcn18 supplies (ldo2_reg/ldo3_reg). On a cold boot
the bridge probes before the tps65217 regulators are registered, so the
bulk supply enable returns -EPROBE_DEFER and the driver core retries
the probe (which then succeeds). The old dev_err() logged this expected
deferral as a KERN_ERR on every boot:

    it66121 0-004c: Failed to enable power supplies

Switch to dev_err_probe() so the deferral is recorded in
/sys/kernel/debug/devices_deferred instead of spamming the console,
while a genuine non-deferred failure is still logged at error level.
Probe behaviour is unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific log-level fix for BeagleBone Black Rev D Qt dashboard]
Signed-off-by: nhat092005 <minhnhat092005@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
index a007b5cbb576..75717205a591 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/ite-it66121.c
@@ -1608,8 +1608,7 @@ static int it66121_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	ret = devm_regulator_bulk_get_enable(dev, ARRAY_SIZE(it66121_supplies),
 					     it66121_supplies);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "Failed to enable power supplies\n");
-		return ret;
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "Failed to enable power supplies\n");
 	}
 	ret = it66121_get_optional_vrf12(dev);
 	if (ret)
-- 
